#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:2
msgid "pwm interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `pwm` interface allows access to a specific PWM channel on a device. The "
"interface is restricted because it provides privileged access to PWM "
"hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"Use `snap interface pwm` to see which PWM devices are available on the "
"system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"$ snap interface pwm\n"
"name: pwm\n"
"summary: allows access to specific PWM channel\n"
"slots:\n"
"- gadget:led-1\n"
"- gadget:led-2\n"
"- gadget:fan-1\n"
"- gadget:fan-2\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:20
msgid "<h2 id='heading--example'>Example</h2>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"With an example snap application called _app_ installed, the following "
"command will connect its PWM interface to the specified PWM device channel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:24
msgid "$  snap connect app:activity-led gadget:led-1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:29
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:31
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:33
msgid ""
"`channel` (slot): PWM device channel number to export and expose to "
"consuming snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:34
msgid "`chip-number` (slot): chip base number to export"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:36
msgid ""
"To use a PWM device, the snap developer must add `plugs:[pwm]` to a "
"snap’s[ snapcraft.yaml](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/"
"reference/project-file/anatomy-of-snapcraft-yaml/). The snap user can then "
"access a specific pwm device with an{ref}` interface connection <explanation-"
"interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:38
msgid ""
"Unless the snap is expected to actually use a set of PWM channels that is "
"not predefined, it is recommended to define distinct plugs for each used pwm "
"channel, like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:40
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  activity-led:\n"
"    interface: pwm\n"
"  warning-led:\n"
"    interface: pwm\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:48
msgid ""
"This has the advantage of being self-documenting and 1-1 connections like "
"these are easier to track and setup with{ref}` auto-connections <explanation-"
"interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`, if the latter is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:50
msgid ""
"When the interface is connected, `\"echo (channel number) > /sys/class/pwm/"
"pwmchipN/export\"` is run internally to enable access to the PWM channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:52
msgid ""
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the device via `/sys/class/pwm/"
"pwmchipN/pwmX` where _N_ is the base of the PWM chip and _X_ is channel "
"number specified by the connected slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:54
msgid ""
"Finally, when the interface is disconnected, `\"echo (channel number) > /sys/"
"class/pwmchipN/unexport\" is run internally to disable access to the PWM "
"channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/pwm-interface.md:56
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

